13. what is libuv?

libuv is a C library that Node.js uses under the hood to handle asynchronous (non-blocking) operations like:
File system tasks (reading/writing files)
Network requests
Timers
Child processes

💡 In simple words:

libuv is the engine that makes Node.js’s event loop and async behavior work.

Even though Node.js runs JavaScript on a single thread, libuv secretly uses a pool of background threads to perform tasks in parallel, so your code doesn’t get blocked.

🧠 What libuv does:

Manages the Event Loop → decides what runs next.

Handles Async I/O → reads files, handles sockets, timers, etc.

Manages Thread Pool → runs slow operations (like file access) in the background.

Provides Cross-Platform Support → works on Windows, macOS, and Linux the same way.

