15. 🌐 What is a REST API? (Simple Explanation)

👉 A REST API is a way for two systems (like a mobile app and a server) to talk to each other over the internet.

🧠 Very Simple Definition

REST API = A set of rules to send and get data using HTTP (like GET, POST, etc.)

📱 Real-Life Example

Think about ordering food on an app 🍔

You (client) → send request: “Give me menu”
Server → sends menu (data)
You → place order
Server → confirms order

👉 This communication happens using a REST API

🔄 How It Works

A REST API uses HTTP methods:

🔹 1. GET (Read data)

👉 “Give me data”

Example:
Get all users

GET /users
🔹 2. POST (Create data)

👉 “Add new data”

Example:
Create a new user

POST /users
🔹 3. PUT (Update data)

👉 “Update existing data”

Example:
Update user details

PUT /users/1
🔹 4. DELETE (Remove data)

👉 “Delete data”

Example:
Delete a user

DELETE /users/1
📦 Data Format
Mostly uses JSON (easy to read)

Example:

{
  "name": "Prem",
  "age": 22
}
🎯 Key Points (Important for Interviews)
REST stands for Representational State Transfer
Uses HTTP methods (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE)
Works on client-server architecture
Data is usually in JSON format
It is stateless (server doesn’t remember previous request)
🧠 1-Line Interview Answer

👉 “A REST API is a way for client and server to communicate over HTTP using standard methods like GET, POST, PUT, and DELETE to perform operations on data.”